    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0382" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg376"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay thinks the prohibition of the importation of firearms of doubtful
                    advantage, but Mr. Rockhill can assent if a practicable scheme for a reasonable
                    renewal term is generally supported by the powers, subject, <pb facs="0383"
                        n="377" xml:id="pg377"/> so far as this Government is concerned, to the
                    necessity of asking express legislation of Congress in case the existing
                    authority of law does not suffice for the execution of our share of the proposed
                    arrangement.</p>
                <p>Mr. Hay is gratified that Mr. Rockhill will remain until August 15.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
